$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ a & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1069 "q-218731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $u$ if  ${u}^{2}+\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16965fbd-f380-5aaa-bd39-b9dfc41f6cc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487296 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${u}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+\\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {u}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ {u}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{10}-\\frac{4}{10} \\\\ {u}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}} \\\\ |u| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}} \\\\ |u| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ |u| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ u & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1069 "q-30226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $t$ where ${t}^{2}=\\frac{16}{9}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b387dd0-04fb-5792-afe0-da3fe94240d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487300 #edb/ref 1074 "We take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}} \\\\ |t| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\ |t| & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1069 "q-218546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${x}^{2}-15=34,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28369a0e-aba7-51eb-8715-45d32f7550f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487308 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${x}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-15 & =34 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |x| & =7 \\\\ x & =\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1069 "q-23833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $z$ if ${z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{50}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40c2d4a4-7047-536a-96ef-5761a02b86db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487318 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${z}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{50} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{50}} \\\\ |z| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{50}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{50}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot 2}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111426" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $w$ where $16{w}^{2}=9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d4e69dd-adb5-5686-b554-16f7f78bb263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487346 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${w}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{w}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {w}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{w}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{16}} \\\\ |w| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\ |w| & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ w & =\\pm \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve  $\\frac{{q}^{2}}{2}-18=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f380333b-76ae-58b4-8fc8-adf9bbb2d3ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487400 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${q}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{q}^{2}}{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{q}^{2}}{2} & =18 \\\\ {q}^{2} & =2\\cdot 18 \\\\ {q}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{q}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\ |q| & =6 \\\\ q & =\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $b$ if ${b}^{2}-15=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe6cba18-c737-5fde-a708-668f780bcd21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487406 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the ${b}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}-15 & =4 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{b}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{19} \\\\ |b| & =\\sqrt{19} \\\\ b & =\\pm \\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
